I'll inspect the existing events/tools components and data shapes so the mockup mirrors the real payloads.Now I have the real payload shape (`message.tool_events[]` with `tool`, `status`, `request`, `response`, `error`, `duration_ms`, plus `lifecycle_events[]`). Here's the scope, contract, and the runnable mockup.

## 1. Screen / flow outline

**Mockup:** `mockups/chat-entry-tools.html` — a live conversation feed rendering the refactored `ChatEntry`.

What must actually work:

| Zone | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| **New one‑line tool strip** (under the header) | Always visible when the message has tools or is streaming. Shows the **last execution**: status icon + tool name + arg preview + duration, plus run totals (`4 tools · 3.2 s · 1 error`). Live‑updates while streaming. |
| **Strip → panel** | Clicking the strip expands the full `ChatMessageEvents` wall inline (all tools, args, errors, expandable request/response, lifecycle). |
| **Header trigger** | Stays: the wrench toggles the same full panel and is reachable while a long message scrolls (header is sticky, the strip is not). Count moved out of the header into the strip. |
| **⋯ Processing details** | Appears *inside* the strip only when expanded → opens the right drawer with full JSON per tool. |
| **Feed states** | loading / empty / error, all reachable from the mock control bar. |
| **Viewport** | `Wide` / `Narrow` (375 px) via a real CSS **container query** on the entry, plus `Channel mode` (transparent headers). |
| **Persistence** | Expanded panels, open tool rows, mode and width survive reload; `Reset mock` clears. |

## 2. Mock API contract

| Method | Path | Purpose / payload |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/chats/c_dev/messages?empty=1\|fail=1` | `Message[]`; `?empty=1` → `[]`, `?fail=1` → 500 |
| POST | `/api/chats/c_dev/messages/:id/tool-events` | appends `{ tool, status, request }` |
| PATCH | `/api/chats/c_dev/messages/:id/tool-events/:toolCallId` | patches `{ status, duration_ms, response, error }` |
| PATCH | `/api/chats/c_dev/messages/:id` | patches `{ done, content, read_by }` |
| DELETE | `/api/chats/c_dev/messages/:id` | removes message |

## 3. The mockup

